{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.StrongRankCondition","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Defs","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3_finrank_eq_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3_finrank_eq_five","kind":"theorem","line":476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L476-L483","doc":"The rank, as a number. `StrongRankCondition` is what makes \"rank\" a\nwell-defined natural number at all; it holds for every nontrivial commutative\nring, and is taken as a hypothesis here rather than derived so that the file\nkeeps its minimal import cone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Basis","kind":"def","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L456-L474","doc":"**`TL₃(δ)` is free of rank five on `{1, e₀, e₁, e₀e₁, e₁e₀}`.**\n\n`dim TL₃(δ) = 5 = catalan 3`, the second instance — after `tl2Basis` — of\n`dim TL_n = catalan n` proved here as an algebra fact rather than read off a\ncount of planar diagrams. The two halves are `tl3_span_eq_top` (upper) and\n`tl3_linearIndependent` (lower). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L422-L454","doc":"**`{1, e₀, e₁, e₀e₁, e₁e₀}` is linearly independent in `TL₃(δ)`** whenever\n`δ` is a unit and `δ² − 1` is a non-zero-divisor.\n\nThe trivial summand does the first step on its own: only `1` has a non-zero\nimage there, so its coefficient dies before the matrix block is touched. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3_matrix_indep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3_matrix_indep","kind":"theorem","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L389-L420","doc":"The independence, done in the matrix block. Reading the four entries in the\norder `(1,1)`, `(0,1)`, `(1,0)`, `(0,0)` makes each coefficient vanish using only\nthe ones already known, so no linear system is ever solved:\n\n* `(1,1)` gives `g₂(δ − c) = 0`; multiplying by `δ` turns it into\n  `g₂(δ² − 1) = 0`, hence `g₂ = 0`;\n* `(0,1)` then reads `g₃ = 0`;\n* `(1,0)` then reads `g₄(δ² − 1) = 0`, hence `g₄ = 0`;\n* `(0,0)` then reads `g₁δ = 0`, and `δ` is a unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Rep5_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Rep5_e","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L384-L387","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Rep5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Rep5","kind":"def","line":378,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L378-L382","doc":"**The five-dimensional representation of `TL₃(δ)`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Fam5_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Fam5_comm","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L374-L376","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Fam5_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Fam5_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L369-L372","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Fam5_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Fam5_sq","kind":"theorem","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L363-L367","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Fam5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3Fam5","kind":"def","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L358-L361","doc":"The `2 × 2` family of `TemperleyLiebAlgebra` summed with the trivial\nrepresentation `e_i ↦ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3M₁_mul_tl3M₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3M₁_mul_tl3M₀","kind":"theorem","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L348-L356","doc":"`M₁M₀`, computed. Its `(1,0)` entry is `δ² − 1` — the quantity the\nnon-degeneracy hypothesis below is about, arriving here on its own rather than\nby assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3M₀_mul_tl3M₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3M₀_mul_tl3M₁","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L340-L346","doc":"`M₀M₁`, computed. The `1`s are `δc`, so this is where `δ` being a unit\nenters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3_span_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl3_span_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L227-L304","doc":"**`TL₃(δ) = span_R {1, e₀, e₁, e₀e₁, e₁e₀}`** — so `dim TL₃(δ) ≤ 5 = catalan 3`.\n\nThis is the upper bound. The matching lower bound is `tl3_linearIndependent`\nbelow, and the two together are `tl3Basis` — so `dim TL₃(δ) = 5` exactly, under\nthe genericity hypotheses stated there.\n\n🛑 **This paragraph used to say freeness was NOT claimable at `n = 3`**, on the\nground that `TemperleyLiebAlgebra`'s `tl3Fam` lands in `2 × 2` matrices — a\n`4`-dimensional target, which indeed cannot witness independence of five\nelements however it is chosen. The obstruction was read correctly and the\nconclusion drawn from it was too strong: the fix is not a different `2 × 2`\nfamily but the *same* one summed with the trivial representation `e_i ↦ 0`,\ngiving a `5`-dimensional target. See `tl3Rep5`.\n\nThe 25 products, for the reader checking the case list is complete: with\n`A = e₀`, `B = e₁`, the interesting ones are `A(BA) = A`, `B(AB) = B`,\n`(AB)(AB) = AB`, `(BA)(BA) = BA` (adjacency), `(AB)(BA) = δ·A`,\n`(BA)(AB) = δ·B` (loop then adjacency), and the rest are a loop relation or an\nidentity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.gens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.gens","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L221-L225","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.bsq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.bsq","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L218-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.asq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.asq","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L217-L217","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.bab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.bab","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L216-L216","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.aba","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.aba","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L215-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.adj10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.adj10","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L213-L213","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.adj01","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.adj01","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L212-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.b3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.b3","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L210-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.a3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.a3","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L209-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.TL3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.TL3","kind":"def","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L206-L207","doc":"`TL₃(δ)`: two generators, and they are adjacent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl2Basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl2Basis","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L170-L187","doc":"**`TL₂(δ) is free of rank two on `{1, e₀}`.**\n\n`TemperleyLiebAlgebra` states this as the classical fact and then says freeness\n\"is not claimed\" there, because it had the lower bound and no upper bound. With\n`tl2_span_eq_top` supplying the upper bound, the two halves meet and the basis\nexists.\n\n`dim TL₂(δ) = 2 = catalan 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl2_linearIndependent'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl2_linearIndependent'","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L153-L168","doc":"**`{1, e₀}` is linearly independent in `TL₂(δ)`**, restated from\n`TemperleyLiebAlgebra.tl2_linearIndependent` in the `LinearIndependent` form\n`Basis.mk` wants. The mathematical content is entirely that lemma's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl2_span_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.tl2_span_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L128-L151","doc":"**`TL₂(δ) = span_R {1, e₀}`.**\n\nThe upper bound `QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebAlgebra` records as absent. With\n`tl2_linearIndependent` from that file this is an exact `dim TL₂(δ) = 2`, which\nis `catalan 2` — the first instance of `dim TL_n = catalan n` here proved as an\n*algebra* fact rather than a count of partitions.\n\nOnly two relations are used, and only one of them non-trivially: `e² = δ·e`\nputs the single interesting product back in the span. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.mul_mem_span_of_pairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.mul_mem_span_of_pairs","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L106-L118","doc":"The multiplication-closure hypothesis, reduced to products of spanning\nelements. `Submodule.span_mul_span` does the work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.eq_top_of_one_mem_of_gen_mem_of_mul_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning.eq_top_of_one_mem_of_gen_mem_of_mul_mem","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebSpanning.lean#L85-L104","doc":"**If a submodule contains `1` and every generator and is closed under\nmultiplication, it is everything.**\n\nThe whole upper-bound method in one lemma. `adjoin_range_e_eq_top` supplies that\nthe generators generate; `Submodule.toSubalgebra` turns the hypotheses into a\nsubalgebra; `Algebra.adjoin_le` closes it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}